From: originaxiom <originaxiom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:51:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 5, patch 13;
 row A of its card): A SENTENCE OF ARRIVAL IS READ AS A READER READS IT

Review 79's two readers planted nine sentences of arrival against the gate `arrival-phrases`, and all nine passed
(R79-SM-44, R79-SM-45, row 25 of main's table). Made again on the commit before this patch: the nine stand in the
patch's test, and the reading that stood before, kept in the test, reports none of them.

Four things let them through:
  - a phrase was looked for as one run of characters on one line. "the Standard Model is now derived", and the
    phrase with a line break inside it, were not found;
  - a word of denial anywhere in the phrase's sentence excused it. "Without a single free parameter, the Standard
    Model is derived." passed on "without", and "There is no doubt: all nineteen are derived." on "no";
  - a word of aim was matched from its start and could run on, so "aimless" excused;
  - the sentence's part before the phrase was cut to its last 160 characters before it was read, and the cut could
    make "claim" into "aim".

The rule is main's, from its M10 and M11, each the stricter option:
  - a word of denial excuses a phrase only in the clause that carries the phrase, and only when it stands before
    the phrase or inside it. A clause ends at a comma, a semicolon, a colon, a bracket or a dash. A clause that
    begins with "that" is read with the clause before it;
  - a word of condition excuses across its sentence;
  - whole words only, and nothing cut.
A phrase is read across white space, one line break and marks of emphasis, and with at most two words inside it.
A place that two phrases fit is reported once.

ONE READING IS THIS SEAT'S AND IS MAIN'S TO CHANGE: a word of aim is read as a word of denial is, in its own
clause and before the phrase. Main's two messages name denial and condition and not aim. Read the other way,
"After years of seeking, the Standard Model is derived." would pass.

ONE ASSERTION OF A TEST OF MAIN'S IS CHANGED, with a dated note in the test
(tests/test_arrival_phrases.py::test_the_advisor_seats_own_sentences_for_its_mend_of_the_same_gate): a sentence
in brackets whose denial stands before a colon was asserted to pass. It has the shape of two of the nine, and is
refused now. It stands on no page.

On main's pages nothing moves: the three old lines keep their keys, because a key is still made as it was made;
the four sentences that were excused are excused by a denial in their own clause; with words read inside a
phrase, five more places are found, and each is excused by a denial or an aim in its own clause. None rests on a
word of condition. The test holds this on the repository itself.

What the reader still passes is held in the test, so that it is not met by surprise: the first of the nine with
its comma taken out, a denial about something else in the phrase's own clause, a word of condition that states
none, and other words than the sixteen phrases. What it refuses though it is honest is held there too: a denial
two clauses back, and an aim before a colon with no "that" after it.

Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it: the nine, with twins.
